# Python 3.14

All code in this project **must** target **Python 3.14**. Local venv, CI, and the runtime image are all 3.14 (`requires-python = ">=3.14"`).

## Source of truth

- Prefer the official docs over memory or older tutorials: [What’s new in Python 3.14](https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.14.html) and the current [Python 3 docs](https://docs.python.org/3/).
- When unsure about syntax, typing, stdlib APIs, or idioms, look up the **3.14** docs and follow current recommendations.
- Do **not** write code for older interpreters (3.11–3.13 workarounds, polyfills, or version checks) unless explicitly required for a third-party constraint.

## Coding practices (3.14)

- Use modern typing: deferred annotation evaluation is the default (PEP 649/749) — no need for `from __future__ import annotations` for forward refs.
- Prefer stdlib 3.14 APIs when they fit (e.g. `compression.zstd`, improved `uuid`, asyncio introspection) over reinventing or pulling in duplicates.
- Use template strings (`t""`, PEP 750) when building strings that need safe/custom processing (e.g. structured logging, escaping); keep `f""` for ordinary formatting.
- Follow language rules added in 3.14 (e.g. do not `return`/`break`/`continue` out of a `finally` — PEP 765).
- Prefer clear, current idioms (built-in generics, `match`/`case` where it improves clarity, Enums over magic strings) over outdated patterns from older Python guides.

## Environment

- Create/run against **Python 3.14** only (`python3.14 -m venv .venv`).
- Activate the project venv before running tests, lint, type-check, or the app (see activate-venv rule).
